  "Question": "In right triangles \\(ABC\\) and \\(DEF\\), \\(\\angle C=\\angle F=90^\\circ\\), \\(AB=DE\\), and \\(BC=EF\\). Which criterion should be used to prove congruence?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "SAS",
    "B": "SSS",
    "C": "AAS",
    "D": "HL"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Both are right triangles. \\(AB\\) and \\(DE\\) are the hypotenuses, and \\(BC\\) and \\(EF\\) are legs. The hypotenuses and one pair of corresponding legs are equal, so use HL.",
